1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,525
NBA Global Reach Hits Record Heights in 2026.

2
00:00:04,475 --> 00:00:17,700
The NBA's international expansion reached unprecedented levels in 2026, with a record 135 international players on opening-night rosters representing 41 countries and territories.

3
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:25,975
Canada led all countries with 25 players, followed by France with 14, Australia with 11, and Nigeria with 8.

4
00:00:25,975 --> 00:00:37,100
The league announced new multiyear partnerships with broadcasters in India, Brazil, and South Africa, bringing total international media rights deals to 215 countries.

5
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:47,475
The regular-season international games series expanded to 16 games played across 12 cities, including debut visits to Mumbai, Nairobi, and Manila.

6
00:00:47,475 --> 00:00:58,112
NBA merchandise sales outside North America grew 34% year-over-year, driven by Wembanyama's jersey in Europe and Shai Gilgeous-Alexander's popularity in Canada.

7
00:00:58,112 --> 00:01:06,362
League Commissioner Adam Silver noted that international viewership now accounts for roughly 40% of the NBA's total global audience.

8
00:01:06,362 --> 00:01:20,087
The growth of grassroots basketball programs funded by the NBA in Africa and Latin America has produced a pipeline of talent that shows no signs of slowing, ensuring the league's international presence will only deepen in the coming years.

